1
00:00:01,440 --> 00:00:07,440
Chapter 34 It was near Christmas by the time war was settled.

2
00:00:08,179 --> 00:00:10,559
The season of general holiday approached.

3
00:00:11,279 --> 00:00:14,334
I now closed Morton's school, taking care that

4
00:00:14,335 --> 00:00:17,941
the parting should not be barren on my side.

5
00:00:18,679 --> 00:00:22,440
Good fortune opens the hand as well as the heart wonderfully.

6
00:00:23,679 --> 00:00:28,267
And to give somewhat when we have largely received is but to

7
00:00:28,269 --> 00:00:32,320
afford a vent to the unusual ebullition of the sensations.

8
00:00:33,539 --> 00:00:40,119
I had long felt with pleasure that many of my rustic scholars liked me, and when we

9
00:00:40,120 --> 00:00:43,724
parted that consciousness was confirmed, they

10
00:00:43,725 --> 00:00:47,440
manifested their affection plainly and strongly.

11
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:51,675
Deep was my gratification to find I had really

12
00:00:51,676 --> 00:00:55,120
a place in their unsophisticated hearts.

13
00:00:55,559 --> 00:01:00,600
I promised them that never a week should pass in future that I did not visit them

14
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:04,059
and give them an hours teaching in their school.

15
00:01:05,559 --> 00:01:11,740
Mr. Rivers came up as, having seen the classes, now numbering 60 girls,

16
00:01:12,360 --> 00:01:14,500
file out before me and locked the door.

17
00:01:15,339 --> 00:01:19,278
I stood with the key in my hand, exchanging a few words of

18
00:01:19,279 --> 00:01:23,119
special farewell with some half-dozen of my best scholars.

19
00:01:24,740 --> 00:01:30,600
As decent, respectable, modest, and well-informed young women as could be

20
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:32,960
found in the ranks of the British peasantry.

21
00:01:33,740 --> 00:01:35,639
And that is saying a great deal.

22
00:01:36,460 --> 00:01:41,440
For after all, the British peasantry are the best taught, best-mannered,

23
00:01:41,779 --> 00:01:43,860
most self-respecting of any in Europe.

24
00:01:44,580 --> 00:01:50,500
Since those days, I have seen pace on this and bow in it, and the best engine of them

25
00:01:50,501 --> 00:01:57,520
seemed to me ignorant, coarse, and besotted, compared with my Morton girls.

26
00:01:57,899 --> 00:02:02,580
Do you consider you have got your reward for a season of exertion?

27
00:02:03,460 --> 00:02:05,320
Ask Mr. Rivers when they were gone.

28
00:02:06,539 --> 00:02:09,449
Does not the consciousness of having done some

29
00:02:09,451 --> 00:02:12,721
real good in your day in generation give pleasure?

30
00:02:15,220 --> 00:02:19,375
And you have only toiled a few months, would not a life

31
00:02:19,376 --> 00:02:23,179
devoted to the task of regenerating your race be well spent?

32
00:02:24,139 --> 00:02:28,139
Yes, I said, but I could not go on forever so.

33
00:02:29,039 --> 00:02:33,559
I want to enjoy my own faculties as well as to cultivate those of other people.

34
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:35,520
I must enjoy them now.

35
00:02:36,220 --> 00:02:38,619
Don't recall either my mind or body to the school.

36
00:02:39,179 --> 00:02:42,139
I am out of it and disposed for full holiday.

37
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:45,080
He looked grave.

38
00:02:46,259 --> 00:02:47,259
What now?

39
00:02:47,679 --> 00:02:49,320
What sudden eagerness is this you events?

40
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:51,080
What are you going to do?

41
00:02:52,479 --> 00:02:58,899
To be active, as active as I can, and first I must beg you to set Hannah at

42
00:02:58,900 --> 00:03:01,279
liberty and get somebody else to wait on you.

43
00:03:02,220 --> 00:03:03,220
Do you want her?

44
00:03:03,679 --> 00:03:06,080
Yes, to go with me to more house.

45
00:03:06,880 --> 00:03:09,782
Diana and Mary will be at home in a week, and I want

46
00:03:09,782 --> 00:03:12,520
to have everything in order against their arrival.

47
00:03:13,699 --> 00:03:14,699
I understand.

48
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:18,660
I thought you were for flying off on some excursion.

49
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:20,360
It is better so.

50
00:03:20,839 --> 00:03:22,100
Hannah shall go with you.

51
00:03:23,479 --> 00:03:25,600
Tell her to be ready by tomorrow then.

52
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:27,880
And here is the schoolroom key.

53
00:03:28,679 --> 00:03:31,460
I will give you the key of my cottage in the morning.

54
00:03:32,220 --> 00:03:33,220
He took it.

55
00:03:34,220 --> 00:03:37,559
You give it up very gleefully, said he.

56
00:03:38,320 --> 00:03:42,800
I don't quite understand your lightheartedness because I cannot tell

57
00:03:42,801 --> 00:03:44,978
what employment you propose to yourself as a

58
00:03:44,979 --> 00:03:47,620
substitute for the one you are relinquishing.

59
00:03:48,339 --> 00:03:52,059
What aim, what purpose, what ambition in life have you now?

60
00:03:53,839 --> 00:03:57,100
My first aim will be to clean down.

61
00:03:58,039 --> 00:04:00,699
Do you comprehend the full force of the expression?

62
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:04,699
To clean down more house from chamber to cellar?

63
00:04:04,940 --> 00:04:08,532
My next to rub it up with beeswax oil, and an

64
00:04:08,533 --> 00:04:12,201
indefinite number of cloths till it glitters again.

65
00:04:12,899 --> 00:04:20,020
My third, to arrange every chair, table, bed, carpet, with mathematical precision.

66
00:04:20,740 --> 00:04:24,067
Afterwards I shall go near to ruin you in coals

67
00:04:24,069 --> 00:04:27,520
and peat to keep up good fires in every room.

68
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:33,820
And lastly, the two days preceding that on which your sisters are expected will be

69
00:04:33,820 --> 00:04:40,419
devoted by Hannah and me to such a beating of eggs, sorting of currents, grating of

70
00:04:40,421 --> 00:04:46,000
spices, compounding of Christmas cakes, chopping up of materials for mince pies,

71
00:04:46,820 --> 00:04:49,679
and solemnizing of other culinary rights.

72
00:04:50,199 --> 00:04:55,360
As words can convey, but an inadequate notion of to the uninitiated like you.

73
00:04:56,440 --> 00:05:01,720
My purpose, in short, is to have all things in an absolutely perfect state of

74
00:05:01,721 --> 00:05:05,403
readiness for Diana and Mary before next Thursday, and my

75
00:05:05,404 --> 00:05:09,339
ambition is to give them a bow ideal of a welcome when they come.

76
00:05:11,039 --> 00:05:15,000
Singin smiled slightly, still he was dissatisfied.

77
00:05:16,679 --> 00:05:19,779
It is all very well for the present, said he.

78
00:05:20,539 --> 00:05:26,320
But seriously, I trust that when the first flush of vivacity is over, you will look a

79
00:05:26,320 --> 00:05:29,440
little higher than domestic endearments and household joys.

80
00:05:30,520 --> 00:05:33,139
The best things the world has, I interrupted.

81
00:05:33,839 --> 00:05:34,880
No, Jane, no.

82
00:05:35,639 --> 00:05:37,360
This world is not the scene of fruition.

83
00:05:38,100 --> 00:05:40,720
Do not attempt to make it so, nor of rest.

84
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:42,800
Do not turn slothful.

85
00:05:43,460 --> 00:05:46,399
I mean, on the contrary, to be busy.

86
00:05:47,820 --> 00:05:50,440
Jane, I excuse you for the present.

87
00:05:51,259 --> 00:05:55,199
Two months grace, I allow you for the full enjoyment of your new position,

88
00:05:56,139 --> 00:05:59,619
and for pleasing yourself with this late found charm of relationship.

89
00:06:00,679 --> 00:06:06,720
But then, I hope you will begin to look beyond more house and morten, and sisterly

90
00:06:06,721 --> 00:06:11,360
society, and the selfish calm and sensual comfort of civilized affluence.

91
00:06:12,119 --> 00:06:15,960
I hope your energies will then once more trouble you with their strength.

92
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:18,460
I looked at him with surprise.

93
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:21,240
Sinjin, I said.

94
00:06:22,300 --> 00:06:25,059
I think you are almost wicked to talk so.

95
00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:30,440
I am disposed to be as content as a queen, and you try to stir me up to restlessness,

96
00:06:31,080 --> 00:06:32,080
to what end?

97
00:06:33,339 --> 00:06:38,559
To the end of turning to profit, the talents which God has committed to

98
00:06:38,561 --> 00:06:45,119
your keeping, and of which he will surely one day demand a strict account.

99
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:49,779
Jane, I shall watch you closely and anxiously.

100
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:51,600
I warn you of that.

101
00:06:52,440 --> 00:06:55,224
And try to restrain the disproportionate fervor with

102
00:06:55,225 --> 00:06:58,199
which you throw yourself into commonplace home pleasures.

103
00:06:59,279 --> 00:07:02,100
Don't cling so tenaciously to ties of the flesh.

104
00:07:03,039 --> 00:07:06,039
Save your constancy and ardour for an adequate cause.

105
00:07:06,940 --> 00:07:10,020
For bear to waste them on trite transient objects.

106
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:12,080
Do you hear Jane?

107
00:07:12,699 --> 00:07:14,960
Yes, just as if you were speaking Greek.

108
00:07:15,679 --> 00:07:18,960
I feel I have adequate cause to be happy, and I will be happy.

109
00:07:19,580 --> 00:07:20,580
Goodbye.

110
00:07:22,380 --> 00:07:27,539
Happy at more house I was, and hard I worked, and so did Hannah.

111
00:07:28,300 --> 00:07:32,520
She was charmed to see how Jovey I could be amidst the bustle of a house turn topsy

112
00:07:32,520 --> 00:07:38,139
turvy, how I could brush, and dust, and clean, and cook.

113
00:07:39,039 --> 00:07:45,179
And really, after a day or two of confusion, worse confounded, it was

114
00:07:45,180 --> 00:07:50,259
delightful by degrees to invoke order from the chaos ourselves had made.

115
00:07:51,699 --> 00:07:56,919
I had previously taken a journey to S to purchase some new furniture.

116
00:07:57,699 --> 00:08:02,740
My cousins, having given me carte blanche to affect what alterations I pleased,

117
00:08:03,199 --> 00:08:06,119
and a sum having been set aside for that purpose.

118
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:12,460
The ordinary sitting room and bedrooms I left much as they were, for I knew Diana

119
00:08:12,460 --> 00:08:18,880
and Mary would derive more pleasure from seeing again the old homely tables and

120
00:08:18,880 --> 00:08:24,000
chairs and beds than from the spectacle of the smartest innovations.

121
00:08:25,440 --> 00:08:29,853
Still, some novelty was necessary, to give to their return

122
00:08:29,854 --> 00:08:32,899
the pick on sea with which I wished it to be invested.

123
00:08:34,320 --> 00:08:39,740
Dark, handsome new carpets and curtains, an arrangement of some carefully selected

124
00:08:39,740 --> 00:08:44,979
antique ornaments in porcelain and bronze, new coverings and mirrors and dressing

125
00:08:44,980 --> 00:08:48,084
cases for the toilet tables, answered the

126
00:08:48,085 --> 00:08:52,061
end, they looked fresh without being glaring.

127
00:08:53,559 --> 00:08:56,929
A spare parlour and bedroom, I re furnished

128
00:08:56,930 --> 00:09:00,580
entirely with old mahogany and crimson upholstery.

129
00:09:01,619 --> 00:09:05,240
I laid canvas on the passage and carpets on the stairs.

130
00:09:06,300 --> 00:09:11,919
When all was finished, I thought more house as complete a model of bright modest

131
00:09:11,921 --> 00:09:16,389
snugness within, as it was at this season, a specimen

132
00:09:16,391 --> 00:09:19,679
of wintery waste and desert dreariness without.

133
00:09:20,779 --> 00:09:23,820
The eventful Thursday, at length, came.

134
00:09:24,779 --> 00:09:30,259
They were expected about dark, and air dusk fires were lit upstairs and below.

135
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:36,441
The kitchen was in perfect room, Hannah and I were dressed, and all was in readiness.

136
00:09:36,720 --> 00:09:37,960
Singen arrived first.

137
00:09:39,020 --> 00:09:43,820
I had entreated him to keep quite clear of the house, till everything was arranged.

138
00:09:44,820 --> 00:09:49,759
And indeed, the bare idea of the commotion, at once sorted and trivial,

139
00:09:50,399 --> 00:09:54,699
going on within its walls, suffice to scare him to astrangement.

140
00:09:55,520 --> 00:09:57,953
He found me in the kitchen, watching the

141
00:09:57,955 --> 00:10:01,180
progress of certain cakes for tea, then baking.

142
00:10:02,399 --> 00:10:08,779
Approaching the hearth, he asked, if I was at last satisfied with housemaids

143
00:10:08,781 --> 00:10:13,057
work, I answered by inviting him to accompany me on

144
00:10:13,058 --> 00:10:16,360
a general inspection of the result of my labours.

145
00:10:17,119 --> 00:10:21,440
With some difficulty, I got him to make the tour of the house.

146
00:10:22,720 --> 00:10:27,940
He just looked in at the doors I opened, and when he had wandered upstairs and

147
00:10:27,941 --> 00:10:32,839
downstairs, he said I must have gone through a great deal of fatigue and

148
00:10:32,841 --> 00:10:38,300
trouble, to have affected such considerable changes in so short a time.

149
00:10:39,399 --> 00:10:42,619
But not as syllable did he utter indicating

150
00:10:42,619 --> 00:10:46,380
pleasure in the improved aspect of his abode.

151
00:10:47,300 --> 00:10:49,139
This silence damped me.

152
00:10:50,179 --> 00:10:53,979
I thought perhaps the alterations had disturbed some old associations he valued.

153
00:10:55,000 --> 00:11:00,539
I inquired whether this was the case, no doubt, in a somewhat crestfallen tone.

154
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:05,220
Not at all, he had on the contrary remarked that

155
00:11:05,221 --> 00:11:08,960
I had scrupulously respected every association.

156
00:11:09,839 --> 00:11:15,059
He feared indeed I must have bestowed more thought on the matter than it was worth.

157
00:11:16,240 --> 00:11:19,024
How many minutes, for instance, had I devoted to

158
00:11:19,024 --> 00:11:24,300
studying the arrangement of this very room by the by?

159
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:27,660
Could I tell him where such a book was?

160
00:11:28,800 --> 00:11:30,440
I showed him the volume on the shelf.

161
00:11:31,160 --> 00:11:33,626
He took it down, and with drawing to his

162
00:11:33,627 --> 00:11:37,941
accustomed window recess, he began to read it.

163
00:11:38,679 --> 00:11:41,139
Now, I did not like this reader.

164
00:11:42,080 --> 00:11:45,619
Shingin was a good man, but I began to feel he had spoken

165
00:11:45,620 --> 00:11:49,580
truth of himself when he said he was hard and cold.

166
00:11:50,479 --> 00:11:54,639
The humanities and amenities of life had no attraction for him.

167
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:57,240
It's peaceful enjoyments, no charm.

168
00:11:57,979 --> 00:12:00,479
Literally, he lived only to aspire.

169
00:12:01,539 --> 00:12:05,274
After what was good and great certainly, but still he

170
00:12:05,274 --> 00:12:08,500
would never rest nor approve of others resting around him.

171
00:12:09,580 --> 00:12:14,279
As I looked at his lofty forehead, still and pale as a white stone,

172
00:12:15,039 --> 00:12:17,139
at his fine liniments fixed in study.

173
00:12:18,139 --> 00:12:21,904
I comprehended all at once that he would hardly make a good

174
00:12:21,906 --> 00:12:25,539
husband, that it would be a trying thing to be his wife.

175
00:12:26,559 --> 00:12:32,020
I understood, as by inspiration, the nature of his love for misoliver.

176
00:12:32,699 --> 00:12:36,720
I agreed with him that it was but a love of the senses.

177
00:12:38,100 --> 00:12:42,699
I comprehended how he should despise himself for the feverish influence it

178
00:12:42,701 --> 00:12:49,199
exercised over him, how he should wish to stifle and destroy it, how he should

179
00:12:49,201 --> 00:12:53,539
mistrust its ever-conducting permanently to his happiness or hers.

180
00:12:54,520 --> 00:13:00,059
I saw he was of the material from which nature hues her heroes, Christian and

181
00:13:00,061 --> 00:13:04,255
pagan, her lawgivers, her statesmen, her conquerors,

182
00:13:04,255 --> 00:13:07,860
a steadfast bullwark for great interests to rest upon.

183
00:13:08,639 --> 00:13:15,479
But, at the fireside, too often a cold, cumbersome, gloomy and out of place.

184
00:13:16,759 --> 00:13:20,119
This parlour is not his sphere, I reflected.

185
00:13:21,119 --> 00:13:23,752
The Himalayan Ridge or Caffrey Bush, even the

186
00:13:23,754 --> 00:13:26,520
plague-cursed guinea-coast swamp would suit him better.

187
00:13:27,479 --> 00:13:30,119
Well, may he assume the calm of domestic life.

188
00:13:31,119 --> 00:13:32,119
It is not his element.

189
00:13:32,979 --> 00:13:35,020
There his faculties stagnate.

190
00:13:35,580 --> 00:13:37,699
They cannot develop or appear to advantage.

191
00:13:38,380 --> 00:13:43,960
It is in scenes of strife and danger, where courage is proved and energy

192
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:51,980
exercised, and fortitude tasked, that he will speak and move the leader and superior.

193
00:13:52,460 --> 00:13:54,979
A merry child would have the advantage of him on this path.

194
00:13:55,699 --> 00:13:57,800
He is right to choose a missionary's career.

195
00:13:58,500 --> 00:13:59,500
I see it now.

196
00:14:00,580 --> 00:14:01,699
They are coming!

197
00:14:02,139 --> 00:14:03,139
They are coming!

198
00:14:03,520 --> 00:14:06,039
cried Hannah, throwing open the parlour door.

199
00:14:06,919 --> 00:14:09,940
At the same moment, old Carlo barked joyfully.

200
00:14:10,919 --> 00:14:11,919
Out I ran.

201
00:14:12,619 --> 00:14:16,059
It was now dark, but a rumbling of wheels was audible.

202
00:14:17,179 --> 00:14:18,720
Hannah soon had a lantern lit.

203
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:21,320
The vehicle had stopped at the wicked.

204
00:14:22,139 --> 00:14:23,940
The driver opened the door.

205
00:14:24,740 --> 00:14:28,619
First one well-known form, then another stepped out.

206
00:14:29,220 --> 00:14:33,596
In a minute, I had my face under their bonnets, in contact

207
00:14:33,597 --> 00:14:38,360
first with Mary's soft cheek, then with Diana's flowing curls.

208
00:14:39,300 --> 00:14:41,059
They laughed, kissed me.

209
00:14:41,339 --> 00:14:47,039
Then Hannah, patted Carlo, who was half wild with delight, asked eagerly if all

210
00:14:47,040 --> 00:14:51,820
was well, and being assured in the affirmative, hastened into the house.

211
00:14:52,380 --> 00:14:55,839
They were stiff with their long and jolting drive

212
00:14:55,839 --> 00:14:59,360
from Whitcross, and chilled with the frosty night air.

213
00:15:00,179 --> 00:15:04,259
But their pleasant countenances expanded to the cheerful firelight.

214
00:15:05,679 --> 00:15:10,520
While the driver and Hannah brought in the boxes, they demanded engine.

215
00:15:11,460 --> 00:15:14,940
At this moment, he advanced from the parlour.

216
00:15:15,979 --> 00:15:19,199
They both threw their arms around his neck at once.

217
00:15:20,139 --> 00:15:26,539
He gave each one quiet kiss, said in a low tone a few words of welcome, stood a while

218
00:15:26,540 --> 00:15:32,460
to be talked to, and then, intimating that he supposed they would soon rejoin him in

219
00:15:32,460 --> 00:15:35,940
the parlour, with drew there as to a place of refuge.

220
00:15:36,699 --> 00:15:40,779
I had lit their candles to go upstairs, but Diana had

221
00:15:40,781 --> 00:15:44,460
first to give hospitable orders respecting the driver.

222
00:15:45,320 --> 00:15:47,880
This done both followed me.

223
00:15:48,960 --> 00:15:53,360
They were delighted with the renovation and decorations of their rooms,

224
00:15:54,179 --> 00:15:59,740
with the new drapery and fresh carpets and rich tinted china vases.

225
00:16:00,539 --> 00:16:03,880
They expressed their gratification ungrudgingly.

226
00:16:05,339 --> 00:16:09,919
I had the pleasure of feeling that my arrangements met their wishes exactly,

227
00:16:10,880 --> 00:16:15,520
and that what I had done added a vivid charm to their joyous return home.

228
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:23,399
Sweet was that evening, my cousins, full of exhilaration, were so eloquent in

229
00:16:23,400 --> 00:16:28,399
narrative and comment that their fluency covered Syngen's taciturnity.

230
00:16:28,820 --> 00:16:32,324
He was sincerely glad to see his sisters, but in their

231
00:16:32,326 --> 00:16:37,039
glow of further and flow of joy he could not sympathize.

232
00:16:38,119 --> 00:16:44,600
The event of the day, that is, the return of Diana and Mary pleased him,

233
00:16:45,139 --> 00:16:48,437
but the accompaniments of that event, the glad

234
00:16:48,437 --> 00:16:51,639
tumult, the garalist glee of reception irked him.

235
00:16:52,419 --> 00:16:54,759
I saw he wished the car memorial was come.

236
00:16:56,100 --> 00:17:01,179
In the very meridian of the night's enjoyment, about an hour after tea,

237
00:17:02,020 --> 00:17:03,539
a wrap was heard at the door.

238
00:17:04,699 --> 00:17:10,720
Hannah entered with the intimation that a poor lad was come, at that unlikely time,

239
00:17:11,199 --> 00:17:14,500
to fetch Mr. Rivers to see his mother, who was drawing away.

240
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:17,039
Where does she live, Hannah?

241
00:17:18,339 --> 00:17:23,220
Clear up at Whitcross Brow, almost four miles off, and more and moss all the way.

242
00:17:24,360 --> 00:17:25,419
Tell him I will go.

243
00:17:26,919 --> 00:17:29,279
I'm sure, sir, you had better not.

244
00:17:30,220 --> 00:17:32,740
It's the worst road to travel after dark that can be.

245
00:17:33,580 --> 00:17:38,860
There's no track at all over the bog, and then it is such a bitter night.

246
00:17:39,479 --> 00:17:41,539
The keenest wind you ever felt.

247
00:17:42,360 --> 00:17:46,220
You had better send words, sir, that you will be there in the morning.

248
00:17:47,479 --> 00:17:50,919
But he was already in the passage, putting on his cloak,

249
00:17:50,921 --> 00:17:54,839
and without one objection, one murmur, he departed.

250
00:17:55,800 --> 00:17:57,699
It was then nine o'clock.

251
00:17:58,559 --> 00:18:03,199
He did not return till midnight, starved and tired enough he was.

252
00:18:04,039 --> 00:18:06,199
But he looked happier than when he set out.

253
00:18:07,020 --> 00:18:12,460
He had performed an act of duty, made an exertion, felt his own strength to

254
00:18:12,460 --> 00:18:15,979
do and deny, and was on better terms with himself.

255
00:18:17,300 --> 00:18:22,100
I am afraid the whole of the ensuing week tried his patience.

256
00:18:23,020 --> 00:18:27,173
It was Christmas week, we took to no settled employment,

257
00:18:27,175 --> 00:18:31,059
but spent it in a sort of merry domestic dissipation.

258
00:18:32,020 --> 00:18:39,080
The air of the moors, the freedom of home, the dawn of prosperity, acted on Diana and

259
00:18:39,081 --> 00:18:41,860
Mary's spirits like some life-giving elixir.

260
00:18:42,699 --> 00:18:47,660
They were gay from morning till noon, and from noon till night.

261
00:18:48,360 --> 00:18:53,080
They could always talk, and their discourse, witty, pithy, original,

262
00:18:53,679 --> 00:18:58,699
had such charms for me that I preferred listening to and sharing in it,

263
00:18:59,199 --> 00:19:00,399
to doing anything else.

264
00:19:01,839 --> 00:19:06,600
Syngin did not rebuke our vivacity, but he escaped from it.

265
00:19:07,339 --> 00:19:12,639
He was seldom in the house, his parish was large, the population scattered,

266
00:19:13,440 --> 00:19:18,820
and he found daily business in visiting the sick and poor in its different districts.

267
00:19:19,639 --> 00:19:24,279
One morning at breakfast, Diana, after looking a little pensive for some

268
00:19:24,281 --> 00:19:29,080
minutes, asked him, if his plans were yet unchanged.

269
00:19:30,059 --> 00:19:37,899
Unchanged and unchangeable was the reply, and he proceeded to inform us that his

270
00:19:37,900 --> 00:19:43,679
departure from England was now definitively fixed for the ensuing year.

271
00:19:44,940 --> 00:19:50,759
And Rosamond Oliver, suggested Mary, the word seeming to escape her lips

272
00:19:50,760 --> 00:19:54,525
involuntarily, for no sooner had she uttered them,

273
00:19:54,527 --> 00:19:57,740
than she made a gesture as if wishing to recall them.

274
00:19:59,160 --> 00:20:02,285
Syngin had a book in his hand, it was his unsocial

275
00:20:02,286 --> 00:20:06,240
custom to read at meals, he closed it, and looked up.

276
00:20:12,100 --> 00:20:17,066
Rosamond Oliver said he, is about to be married

277
00:20:17,067 --> 00:20:21,100
to Mr. Granby, one of the best Rick Granby.

278
00:20:22,039 --> 00:20:24,419
I had the intelligence from her father yesterday.

279
00:20:25,440 --> 00:20:30,320
His sisters looked at each other, and at me, we all three looked at him,

280
00:20:30,960 --> 00:20:32,220
he was serene as glass.

281
00:20:34,339 --> 00:20:36,794
The match must have been got up hastily, said

282
00:20:36,796 --> 00:20:39,880
Diana, they cannot have known each other long.

283
00:20:40,800 --> 00:20:44,679
But two months, they met in October at the county ball at S.

284
00:20:45,759 --> 00:20:50,960
But where there are no obstacles to a union, as in the present case,

285
00:20:51,839 --> 00:20:56,740
where the connection is in every point desirable, delays are unnecessary,

286
00:20:57,580 --> 00:20:59,639
they will be married as soon as S.

287
00:20:59,720 --> 00:21:02,437
or Marn's place, which Sir Frederick gives up

288
00:21:02,437 --> 00:21:05,721
to them, can be refitted for their reception.

289
00:21:06,740 --> 00:21:11,796
The first time I found Syngin alone after this communication,

290
00:21:11,797 --> 00:21:15,220
I felt tempted to inquire if the event distressed him.

291
00:21:16,179 --> 00:21:18,660
But he seemed so little to need sympathy.

292
00:21:19,580 --> 00:21:26,020
That, so far from venturing to offer him more, I experienced some shame at the

293
00:21:26,020 --> 00:21:28,300
recollection of what I had already hazarded.

294
00:21:28,960 --> 00:21:32,520
Besides, I was out of practice in talking to him.

295
00:21:33,220 --> 00:21:39,160
His reserve was again frozen over, and my frankness was congealed beneath it.

296
00:21:39,880 --> 00:21:43,380
He had not kept his promise of treating me like his sisters.

297
00:21:44,440 --> 00:21:48,630
He continually made little chilling differences between us,

298
00:21:48,630 --> 00:21:52,559
which did not at all tend to the development of cordiality.

299
00:21:52,899 --> 00:21:59,660
In short, now that I was acknowledged his kin's woman, and lived under the same roof

300
00:21:59,660 --> 00:22:03,876
with him, I felt the distance between us to be far greater

301
00:22:03,877 --> 00:22:07,419
than when he had known me only as the village school mistress.

302
00:22:08,580 --> 00:22:12,319
When I remembered how far I had once been admitted to his

303
00:22:12,320 --> 00:22:16,080
confidence, I could hardly comprehend his present fragility.

304
00:22:17,919 --> 00:22:22,720
Such being the case, I felt not a little surprised when he raised his head suddenly

305
00:22:22,721 --> 00:22:27,240
from the desk over which he was stooping and said, you see, Jane.

306
00:22:28,119 --> 00:22:31,240
The battle is fought, and the victory won.

307
00:22:32,619 --> 00:22:36,080
Startled at being thus addressed, I did not immediately reply.

308
00:22:36,720 --> 00:22:41,419
After a moment's hesitation, I answered, but are you sure you are not in the

309
00:22:41,421 --> 00:22:45,380
position of those conquerors whose triumphs have cost them too dear?

310
00:22:46,600 --> 00:22:48,279
Would not such another ruin you?

311
00:22:49,059 --> 00:22:53,059
I think not, and if I were, it does not much signify.

312
00:22:53,800 --> 00:22:56,039
I shall never be called upon to contend for such another.

313
00:22:56,520 --> 00:22:58,399
The event of the conflict is decisive.

314
00:22:59,220 --> 00:23:00,500
My way is now clear.

315
00:23:01,240 --> 00:23:02,279
I thank God for it.

316
00:23:03,479 --> 00:23:06,460
So saying, he returned to his papers and his silence.

317
00:23:07,899 --> 00:23:14,520
As our mutual happiness, that is, Diana's, Mary's and mine, settled into a

318
00:23:14,520 --> 00:23:18,839
quieter character, and we resumed our usual habits and regular studies.

319
00:23:19,580 --> 00:23:21,559
Syngin stayed more at home.

320
00:23:22,360 --> 00:23:25,600
He sat with us in the same room, sometimes for hours together.

321
00:23:26,580 --> 00:23:31,125
While Mary drew, Diana pursued a course of encyclopedic

322
00:23:31,126 --> 00:23:34,699
reading she had to my awe and amazement undertaken.

323
00:23:35,279 --> 00:23:41,419
And I fagged away at German, he pondered a mystic law of his own, that of some

324
00:23:41,421 --> 00:23:46,399
eastern tongue, the acquisition of which he thought necessary to his plans.

325
00:23:47,899 --> 00:23:55,039
Thus engaged, he appeared, sitting in his own recess, quiet and absorbed enough.

326
00:23:56,000 --> 00:24:00,759
But that blue eye of his, had a habit of leaving the outlandish-looking grammar,

327
00:24:01,380 --> 00:24:05,175
and wandering over and sometimes fixing upon us, his

328
00:24:05,176 --> 00:24:09,080
fellow students, with a curious intensity of observation.

329
00:24:09,860 --> 00:24:12,800
If caught, it would be instantly withdrawn.

330
00:24:13,500 --> 00:24:18,320
Yet ever and a non, it returned searchingly to our table.

331
00:24:19,240 --> 00:24:20,440
I wondered what it meant.

332
00:24:21,339 --> 00:24:26,199
I wondered too, at the punctual satisfaction he never failed to exhibit,

333
00:24:26,779 --> 00:24:31,096
on an occasion that seemed to me of small moment,

334
00:24:31,097 --> 00:24:34,240
namely, my weekly visit to Morton's school.

335
00:24:35,059 --> 00:24:40,679
And still more was I puzzled when, if the day was unfavorable, if there was

336
00:24:40,680 --> 00:24:47,279
snow or rain or high wind, and his sisters urged me not to go, he would invariably

337
00:24:47,281 --> 00:24:50,713
make light of their solicitude, and encourage me to

338
00:24:50,714 --> 00:24:54,080
accomplish the task without regard to the elements.

339
00:24:55,479 --> 00:25:00,100
Jane is not such a weakling as you would make her, he would say.

340
00:25:00,660 --> 00:25:04,539
She can bear a mountain blast, or a shower, or a few flakes of snow,

341
00:25:04,660 --> 00:25:05,880
as well as any of us.

342
00:25:06,960 --> 00:25:12,240
Her constitution is both sound and elastic, better calculated to endure

343
00:25:12,240 --> 00:25:14,919
variations of climate than many more robust.

344
00:25:15,919 --> 00:25:21,539
And when I returned, sometimes, a good deal tired, and not a little

345
00:25:21,540 --> 00:25:27,500
weather -beaten, I never dared complain, because I saw that Timurma would be to vex

346
00:25:27,501 --> 00:25:33,720
him, on all occasions fortitude pleased him, the reverse was a special annoyance.

347
00:25:34,759 --> 00:25:40,779
One afternoon, however, I got leave to stay at home, because I really had a cold.

348
00:25:42,220 --> 00:25:46,639
His sisters were gone to Morton in my stead, I sat reading Schiller,

349
00:25:47,279 --> 00:25:50,880
he deciphering his crabbed oriental scrolls.

350
00:25:51,479 --> 00:25:55,720
As I exchanged a translation for an exercise, I happened to look his way,

351
00:25:56,240 --> 00:26:00,940
there I found myself under the influence of the ever-watchful blue eye.

352
00:26:01,820 --> 00:26:05,919
How long it had been searching me through and through and over and over,

353
00:26:06,039 --> 00:26:07,039
I cannot tell.

354
00:26:07,679 --> 00:26:13,039
So keen was it, and yet so cold, I felt for the moment superstitious,

355
00:26:13,679 --> 00:26:15,979
as if I was sitting in the room with something uncanny.

356
00:26:17,279 --> 00:26:18,919
Chain, what are you doing?

357
00:26:20,020 --> 00:26:26,100
Learning German, I want you to give up German and learn Hindostani, you are not

358
00:26:26,100 --> 00:26:33,419
in earnest, in such earnest that I must have it so, and I will tell you why.

359
00:26:34,919 --> 00:26:37,505
He then went on to explain that Hindostani was

360
00:26:37,506 --> 00:26:40,960
the language he was himself at present studying.

361
00:26:41,440 --> 00:26:48,080
That, as he advanced, he was apt to forget the commencement, that it would assist him

362
00:26:48,081 --> 00:26:53,500
greatly to have a pupil with whom he might again and again go over the elements,

363
00:26:54,360 --> 00:26:56,919
and so fix them thoroughly in his mind.

364
00:26:57,559 --> 00:27:03,300
That his choice had hovered for some time between me and his sisters, but that he

365
00:27:03,301 --> 00:27:08,779
had fixed on me because he saw I could sit at a task the longest of the three.

366
00:27:09,460 --> 00:27:11,199
Would I do him this favor?

367
00:27:12,440 --> 00:27:16,142
I should not, perhaps, have to make the sacrifice long,

368
00:27:16,144 --> 00:27:19,639
as it wanted now barely three months to his departure.

369
00:27:21,020 --> 00:27:23,800
Singen was not a man to be lightly refused.

370
00:27:24,580 --> 00:27:28,322
You felt that every impression made on him, either for pain

371
00:27:28,323 --> 00:27:32,259
or pleasure was deep -graved and permanent, I consented.

372
00:27:33,020 --> 00:27:36,258
When Diana and Mary returned, the former found

373
00:27:36,259 --> 00:27:39,000
her scholar transferred from her to her brother.

374
00:27:39,380 --> 00:27:42,812
She laughed, and both she and Mary agreed that Singen

375
00:27:42,813 --> 00:27:45,660
should never have persuaded them to such a step.

376
00:27:46,479 --> 00:27:47,580
He answered quietly.

377
00:27:49,539 --> 00:27:50,660
I know it.

378
00:27:52,119 --> 00:27:57,300
I found him a very patient, very forebearing, and yet an exacting master.

379
00:27:58,039 --> 00:27:59,979
He expected me to do a great deal.

380
00:28:01,039 --> 00:28:05,081
And when I fulfilled his expectations, he, in

381
00:28:05,081 --> 00:28:08,900
his own way, fully testified his approbation.

382
00:28:09,380 --> 00:28:12,745
By degrees, he acquired a certain influence

383
00:28:12,747 --> 00:28:15,720
over me that took away my liberty of mind.

384
00:28:16,339 --> 00:28:20,500
His praise and notice were more restraining than his indifference.

385
00:28:21,960 --> 00:28:27,639
I could no longer talk or laugh freely when he was by, because a tire-sumly

386
00:28:27,641 --> 00:28:31,239
important at instinct reminded me that vivacity,

387
00:28:31,240 --> 00:28:34,820
at least in me, was distasteful to him.

388
00:28:35,300 --> 00:28:40,320
I was so fully aware that only serious moods and occupations were acceptable,

389
00:28:41,059 --> 00:28:45,919
that in his presence, every effort to sustain or follow any other became vain.

390
00:28:46,580 --> 00:28:48,759
I fell under a freezing spell.

391
00:28:49,440 --> 00:28:55,059
When he said, go, I went, come, I came, do this, I did it.

392
00:28:55,699 --> 00:28:57,720
But I did not love my servitude.

393
00:28:58,380 --> 00:29:00,199
I wished many a time.

394
00:29:00,639 --> 00:29:02,160
He had continued to neglect me.

395
00:29:02,860 --> 00:29:08,039
One evening when, at bedtime, his sisters and I stood round him, bidding him good

396
00:29:08,040 --> 00:29:11,000
night, he kissed each of them, as was his custom.

397
00:29:11,639 --> 00:29:16,100
And, as was equally his custom, he gave me his hand.

398
00:29:17,139 --> 00:29:20,304
Diana, who chanced to be in a frolic sum humour,

399
00:29:20,304 --> 00:29:23,520
she was not painfully controlled by his will.

400
00:29:23,679 --> 00:29:30,279
For hers, in another way, was a strong, exclaimed, Sinjin, you used to call Jane

401
00:29:30,281 --> 00:29:33,020
your third sister, but you don't treat her as such.

402
00:29:33,580 --> 00:29:34,639
You should kiss her too.

403
00:29:36,119 --> 00:29:37,699
She pushed me towards him.

404
00:29:39,199 --> 00:29:43,559
I thought Diana very provoking and felt uncomfortably confused.

405
00:29:44,240 --> 00:29:48,419
And while I was thus thinking and feeling, Sinjin bent his head.

406
00:29:49,399 --> 00:29:51,919
His Greek face was brought to a level with mine.

407
00:29:52,619 --> 00:29:55,160
His eyes questioned my eyes piercingly.

408
00:29:55,919 --> 00:29:56,919
He kissed me.

409
00:29:57,460 --> 00:30:03,080
There are no such things as marble kisses or ice kisses, or I should say my

410
00:30:03,081 --> 00:30:08,320
ecclesiastical cousin's salute belonged to one of these classes, but there may be

411
00:30:08,320 --> 00:30:11,940
experiment kisses, and his was an experiment kiss.

412
00:30:13,059 --> 00:30:16,100
When given, he viewed me to learn the result.

413
00:30:16,800 --> 00:30:17,860
It was not striking.

414
00:30:18,339 --> 00:30:19,460
I'm sure I did not blush.

415
00:30:20,220 --> 00:30:23,664
Perhaps I might have turned a little pale, for I felt

416
00:30:23,664 --> 00:30:26,880
as if this kiss were a seal affixed to my fetters.

417
00:30:27,520 --> 00:30:32,800
He never omitted the ceremony afterwards, and the gravity and quiescence with which

418
00:30:32,801 --> 00:30:37,119
I underwent it seemed to invest it for him, with a certain charm.

419
00:30:38,179 --> 00:30:45,160
As for me, I daily wished more to please him, but to do so, I felt daily more and

420
00:30:45,160 --> 00:30:52,000
more that I must disown half my nature, stifle half my faculties, rest my tastes

421
00:30:52,001 --> 00:30:56,111
from their original bent, force myself to the adoption

422
00:30:56,111 --> 00:30:59,759
of pursuits for which I had no natural vocation.

423
00:31:00,479 --> 00:31:04,300
He wanted to train me to an elevation I could never reach.

424
00:31:05,119 --> 00:31:09,199
It racked me hourly to aspire to the standard he uplifted.

425
00:31:10,039 --> 00:31:15,720
The thing was as impossible as to mold my irregular features to his correct and

426
00:31:15,721 --> 00:31:18,985
classic pattern, to give to my changeable green

427
00:31:18,986 --> 00:31:22,419
eyes the sea-blue tint and solemn lustre of his own.

428
00:31:23,699 --> 00:31:27,600
Not his ascendancy alone, however, held me in thrall at present.

429
00:31:28,759 --> 00:31:31,619
Of late, it had been easy enough for me to look sad.

430
00:31:32,800 --> 00:31:37,039
A cancoring evil sat at my heart and drained my happiness at its source,

431
00:31:37,899 --> 00:31:39,300
the evil of suspense.

432
00:31:41,020 --> 00:31:44,706
Perhaps you think I had forgotten Mr. Rochester, reader,

433
00:31:44,707 --> 00:31:48,460
amidst these changes of place and fortune, not for a moment.

434
00:31:49,639 --> 00:31:54,600
His idea was still with me, because it was not a vapor sunshine could disperse,

435
00:31:55,139 --> 00:31:58,419
nor a sand-traced effigy storms could wash away.

436
00:31:59,339 --> 00:32:05,820
It was a name graven on a tablet, fated to last as long as the marble it inscribed.

437
00:32:06,580 --> 00:32:10,979
The craving to know what had become of him followed me everywhere.

438
00:32:11,679 --> 00:32:16,160
When I was at Morton, I re-entered my cottage every evening to think of that.

439
00:32:17,199 --> 00:32:22,679
And now, at Morehouse, I sought my bedroom each night to brood over it.

440
00:32:23,860 --> 00:32:27,720
In the course of my necessary correspondence with Mr. Briggs about the

441
00:32:27,721 --> 00:32:31,332
will, I had inquired if he knew anything of

442
00:32:31,334 --> 00:32:35,399
Mr. Rochester's present residence and state of health.

443
00:32:36,339 --> 00:32:42,721
But, as Singen had conjectured, he was quite ignorant of all concerning him.

444
00:32:43,020 --> 00:32:47,580
I then wrote to Mrs. Fairfax, in treating information on the subject.

445
00:32:48,320 --> 00:32:52,520
I had calculated with certainty on this step, answering my end.

446
00:32:53,679 --> 00:32:56,320
I felt sure it would elicit an early answer.

447
00:32:57,699 --> 00:33:02,820
I was astonished when a fortnight passed without reply, but when two months wore

448
00:33:02,820 --> 00:33:06,544
away and day after day the post arrived and brought

449
00:33:06,546 --> 00:33:09,800
nothing for me, I fell afraid of the keenest anxiety.

450
00:33:10,520 --> 00:33:11,520
I wrote again.

451
00:33:12,160 --> 00:33:14,839
There was a chance of my first letter having missed.

452
00:33:15,539 --> 00:33:18,059
Renewed hope followed renewed effort.

453
00:33:18,820 --> 00:33:22,399
It shone like the former for some weeks, then, like it

454
00:33:22,400 --> 00:33:26,059
it faded flickered not a line, not a word reached me.

455
00:33:27,080 --> 00:33:30,509
When half a year wasted in vain expectancy,

456
00:33:30,509 --> 00:33:33,581
my hope died out, and then I felt dark indeed.

457
00:33:34,699 --> 00:33:38,199
A fine spring shone round me, which I could not enjoy.

458
00:33:39,080 --> 00:33:40,080
Summer approached.

459
00:33:40,919 --> 00:33:42,020
Diana tried to cheer me.

460
00:33:42,720 --> 00:33:46,160
She said I looked ill and wished to accompany me to the seaside.

461
00:33:47,100 --> 00:33:48,699
This Singen opposed.

462
00:33:49,800 --> 00:33:51,800
He said I did not want dissipation.

463
00:33:52,039 --> 00:33:53,100
I wanted employment.

464
00:33:53,899 --> 00:33:56,460
My present life was too purposeless.

465
00:33:56,979 --> 00:33:58,039
I required an aim.

466
00:33:59,220 --> 00:34:05,320
And I suppose, by way of supplying deficiencies, he prolonged still further

467
00:34:05,320 --> 00:34:10,440
my lessons in Hindostani and grew more urgent in requiring their accomplishment.

468
00:34:11,240 --> 00:34:14,740
And I, like a fool, never thought of resisting him.

469
00:34:15,479 --> 00:34:17,220
I could not resist him.

470
00:34:18,580 --> 00:34:22,559
One day, I had come to my studies in lower spirits than usual.

471
00:34:24,039 --> 00:34:28,199
The Ebb was occasioned by a poignantly felt disappointment.

472
00:34:29,160 --> 00:34:32,539
Hannah had told me in the morning there was a letter for me.

473
00:34:33,380 --> 00:34:36,823
And when I went down to take it, almost certain that

474
00:34:36,823 --> 00:34:40,339
the long looked for tidings were vouchsafed me at last.

475
00:34:41,320 --> 00:34:44,440
I found only an unimportant note from Mr. Briggs on business.

476
00:34:45,800 --> 00:34:49,039
The bitter check had rung from me some tears.

477
00:34:50,080 --> 00:34:54,638
And now, as I sat, pouring over the crabbed characters and

478
00:34:54,638 --> 00:34:59,899
flourishing tropes of an Indian scribe, my eyes filled again.

479
00:35:01,600 --> 00:35:03,619
Singen called me to his side to read.

480
00:35:04,380 --> 00:35:06,919
In attempting to do this, my voice failed me.

481
00:35:07,639 --> 00:35:09,380
Words were lost in sobs.

482
00:35:10,179 --> 00:35:12,440
He and I were the only occupants of the parlour.

483
00:35:13,300 --> 00:35:15,600
Diana was practising her music in the drawing room.

484
00:35:16,720 --> 00:35:17,820
Mary was gardening.

485
00:35:18,779 --> 00:35:22,880
It was a very fine May day, clear, sunny, and breezy.

486
00:35:23,779 --> 00:35:26,506
My companion expressed no surprise at this

487
00:35:26,508 --> 00:35:29,460
emotion, nor did he question me as to its cause.

488
00:35:30,119 --> 00:35:36,020
He only said, We will wait a few minutes, Jane, till you are more composed.

489
00:35:38,259 --> 00:35:43,220
And while I smothered the paroxysm with all haste, he sat calm and patient,

490
00:35:44,059 --> 00:35:48,899
leaning on his desk and looking like a physician watching with the eye of science

491
00:35:48,900 --> 00:35:53,759
and expected and fully understood crisis in a patient's melody.

492
00:35:55,100 --> 00:36:00,500
Having stifled my sobs, wiped my eyes, and muttered something about not being

493
00:36:00,501 --> 00:36:05,559
very well that morning, I resumed my task and succeeded in completing it.

494
00:36:06,639 --> 00:36:12,600
Singin put away my books and his, locked his desk and said, Now,

495
00:36:13,100 --> 00:36:15,899
Jane, you shall take a walk and with me.

496
00:36:17,080 --> 00:36:18,559
I will call Diana and Mary.

497
00:36:19,440 --> 00:36:23,740
No, I want only one companion this morning, and that must be you.

498
00:36:24,679 --> 00:36:25,679
Put on your things.

499
00:36:26,240 --> 00:36:27,399
Go out by the kitchen door.

500
00:36:28,240 --> 00:36:30,440
Take the road towards the head of Marsh Glen.

501
00:36:31,320 --> 00:36:32,559
I will join you in a moment.

502
00:36:33,860 --> 00:36:35,259
I know no medium.

503
00:36:36,119 --> 00:36:40,660
I never in my life have known any medium in my dealings with positive, hard

504
00:36:40,660 --> 00:36:47,839
characters antagonistic to my own between absolute submission and determined revolt.

505
00:36:49,220 --> 00:36:54,759
I have always faithfully observed the one, up to the very moment of bursting,

506
00:36:55,639 --> 00:36:58,679
sometimes with volcanic vehement into the other.

507
00:36:59,320 --> 00:37:02,301
And as neither present circumstances warranted,

508
00:37:02,301 --> 00:37:05,460
nor my present mood inclined me to mutiny.

509
00:37:05,860 --> 00:37:11,220
I observed careful obedience to Singin's directions, and in ten minutes,

510
00:37:11,860 --> 00:37:16,380
I was treading the wild track of the Glen, side by side with him.

511
00:37:17,419 --> 00:37:19,080
The breeze was from the west.

512
00:37:19,679 --> 00:37:23,440
It came over the hills, sweet with sense of heath and rush.

513
00:37:24,399 --> 00:37:26,360
The sky was of stainless blue.

514
00:37:27,259 --> 00:37:31,660
The stream descending the ravine, swelled with past spring rains,

515
00:37:32,559 --> 00:37:37,039
poured along plentiful and clear, catching golden gleams from the sun,

516
00:37:37,699 --> 00:37:39,479
and sapphire tints from the firmament.

517
00:37:40,839 --> 00:37:45,880
As we advanced and left the track, we trot a soft turf, mossy fine and

518
00:37:45,880 --> 00:37:49,558
emerald green, minutely enameled with a tiny white

519
00:37:49,558 --> 00:37:52,779
flower and spangled with a star -like yellow blossom.

520
00:37:53,600 --> 00:37:58,259
The hills' meantime shut us quite in, for the Glen, towards its head,

521
00:37:58,779 --> 00:38:00,259
wound to their very core.

522
00:38:05,080 --> 00:38:13,080
Let us rest here, said Singin, as we reach the first stragglers of a

523
00:38:13,081 --> 00:38:19,139
waterfall, and where, still a little farther, the mountains shook off turf and

524
00:38:19,141 --> 00:38:25,619
flower, had only heath for raiment and crag for gem, where it exaggerated the

525
00:38:25,620 --> 00:38:31,179
wild to the savage and exchanged the fresh for the frowning, where it guarded the

526
00:38:31,180 --> 00:38:35,179
fallon hope of solitude and a last refuge for silence.

527
00:38:35,880 --> 00:38:37,059
I took a seat.

528
00:38:38,119 --> 00:38:39,279
Singin stood near me.

529
00:38:40,220 --> 00:38:42,199
He looked up the pass and down the hollow.

530
00:38:43,080 --> 00:38:46,653
His glance wandered away with the stream, and returned

531
00:38:46,653 --> 00:38:49,940
to traverse the unclouded heaven which coloured it.

532
00:38:50,740 --> 00:38:51,899
He removed his hat.

533
00:38:52,740 --> 00:38:55,399
Let the breeze stir his hair and kiss his brow.

534
00:38:56,419 --> 00:38:59,139
He seemed in communion with the genius of the haunt.

535
00:38:59,800 --> 00:39:03,080
With his eye he bared farewell to something.

536
00:39:04,080 --> 00:39:09,740
And I shall see it again, he said in dreams when I sleep by the ganges,

537
00:39:10,460 --> 00:39:14,005
and again in a more remote hour when another slumber

538
00:39:14,005 --> 00:39:16,839
overcomes me on the shore of a darker stream.

539
00:39:18,080 --> 00:39:24,380
Strange words of a strange love, an austere patriot's passion for his fatherland.

540
00:39:24,600 --> 00:39:25,600
He sat down.

541
00:39:26,080 --> 00:39:30,460
For half an hour we never spoke, neither he to me nor I to him.

542
00:39:31,199 --> 00:39:34,500
That interval passed, he recommenced.

543
00:39:35,300 --> 00:39:37,380
Jane, I go in six weeks.

544
00:39:38,199 --> 00:39:42,100
I have taken my birth in an east indian man which sails on the 20th of June.

545
00:39:43,240 --> 00:39:44,320
God will protect you.

546
00:39:44,919 --> 00:39:47,679
For you have undertaken his work, I answered.

547
00:39:48,800 --> 00:39:50,320
Yes, said he.

548
00:39:51,339 --> 00:39:53,440
There is my glory and joy.

549
00:39:54,360 --> 00:39:56,880
I am the servant of an infallible master.

550
00:39:57,600 --> 00:40:00,736
I am not going out under human guidance, subject to the

551
00:40:00,736 --> 00:40:04,639
defective laws and air in control of my feeble fellow-worms.

552
00:40:05,440 --> 00:40:10,699
My king, my lawgiver, my captain, is the all-perfect.

553
00:40:11,559 --> 00:40:14,831
It seems strange to me that all around me do not burn to

554
00:40:14,832 --> 00:40:18,419
enlist under the same banner, to join in the same enterprise.

555
00:40:19,520 --> 00:40:22,417
All have not your powers, and it would be folly

556
00:40:22,418 --> 00:40:25,820
for the feeble to wish to march with the strong.

557
00:40:27,020 --> 00:40:29,960
I do not speak to the feeble or think of them.

558
00:40:30,740 --> 00:40:35,500
I address only such as our worthy of the work and competent to accomplish it.

559
00:40:36,899 --> 00:40:40,139
Those are few in number and difficult to discover.

560
00:40:41,559 --> 00:40:48,080
You say truly, but when found, it is right to stir them up, to urge and

561
00:40:48,081 --> 00:40:52,839
exhort them to the effort, to show them what their gifts are and why they were

562
00:40:52,841 --> 00:40:56,119
given, to speak heaven's message in their ear.

563
00:40:56,880 --> 00:41:02,020
To offer them, direct from God, a place in the ranks of his chosen.

564
00:41:03,500 --> 00:41:07,100
If they are really qualified for the task, will not

565
00:41:07,101 --> 00:41:10,240
their own hearts be the first to inform them of it?

566
00:41:11,259 --> 00:41:17,660
I felt, as if an awful charm was framing round and gathering over me, I trembled to

567
00:41:17,660 --> 00:41:22,740
hear some fatal words spoken, which would at once declare and rivet the spell.

568
00:41:23,720 --> 00:41:26,899
And what does your heart say, demanded sinjin?

569
00:41:28,699 --> 00:41:34,119
My heart is mute, my heart is mute, I answered, struck and thrilled.

570
00:41:35,059 --> 00:41:39,500
Then I must speak for it, continued the deep, relentless voice.

571
00:41:40,380 --> 00:41:45,220
Jane, come with me to India, come as my help meet and fellow labourer.

572
00:41:46,100 --> 00:41:52,720
The Glen and Sky spun round, the hills heaved, it was as if I had heard a summons

573
00:41:52,721 --> 00:41:57,779
from heaven, as if a visionary messenger like him of Macedonia had announced,

574
00:41:58,380 --> 00:42:00,119
come over and help us.

575
00:42:00,779 --> 00:42:06,460
But I was no apostle, I could not behold the herald, I could not receive his call.

576
00:42:07,919 --> 00:42:12,300
Oh sinjin, I cried, have some mercy.

577
00:42:13,380 --> 00:42:16,589
I appealed to one who, in the discharge of what he

578
00:42:16,589 --> 00:42:20,300
believed his duty, knew neither mercy nor remorse.

579
00:42:21,000 --> 00:42:25,919
He continued, God and nature intended you for a missionary's wife.

580
00:42:26,559 --> 00:42:30,220
It is not personal, but mental endowments they have given you.

581
00:42:30,979 --> 00:42:32,860
You are formed for labour, not for love.

582
00:42:33,740 --> 00:42:36,440
A missionary's wife you must, shall be.

583
00:42:37,119 --> 00:42:43,460
You shall be mine, I claim you, not for my pleasure but for my sovereign service.

584
00:42:44,399 --> 00:42:48,300
I am not fit for it, I have no vocation, I said.

585
00:42:49,440 --> 00:42:52,300
He had calculated on these first objections.

586
00:42:53,279 --> 00:42:58,979
He was not irritated by them, indeed, as he leaned back against the crag behind

587
00:42:58,980 --> 00:43:03,300
him, folded his arms on his chest and fixed his countenance.

588
00:43:03,759 --> 00:43:09,119
I saw he was prepared for a long and trying opposition, and had taken in a

589
00:43:09,120 --> 00:43:11,660
stock of patience to last him to its close.

590
00:43:12,660 --> 00:43:17,300
Resolved however, that that close should be conquest for him.

591
00:43:18,919 --> 00:43:23,679
Humility Jane said he, is the groundwork of Christian virtues.

592
00:43:24,740 --> 00:43:30,619
You say right that you are not fit for the work, who is fit for it, or who,

593
00:43:31,080 --> 00:43:35,440
that ever was truly called, believed himself worthy of the summons.

594
00:43:36,039 --> 00:43:39,139
I, for instance, am but dust and ashes.

595
00:43:40,100 --> 00:43:43,919
With Saint Paul, I acknowledge myself the chiefest of sinners.

596
00:43:44,860 --> 00:43:49,279
But I do not suffer this sense of my personal vileness to taunt me.

597
00:43:50,020 --> 00:43:54,539
I know my leader, that he is just as well as mighty.

598
00:43:55,539 --> 00:43:59,380
And while he has chosen a feeble instrument to perform a great task,

599
00:43:59,380 --> 00:44:03,771
he will, from the boundless stores of his providence,

600
00:44:03,773 --> 00:44:07,279
supply the inadequacy of the means to the end.

601
00:44:07,960 --> 00:44:09,059
Think like me, Jane.

602
00:44:09,960 --> 00:44:10,960
Trust like me.

603
00:44:11,500 --> 00:44:13,880
It is the rock of ages I ask you to lean on.

604
00:44:14,759 --> 00:44:18,600
Do not doubt, but it will bear the weight of your human weakness.

605
00:44:19,759 --> 00:44:22,020
I do not understand a missionary life.

606
00:44:22,860 --> 00:44:25,139
I have never studied missionary labors.

607
00:44:25,860 --> 00:44:30,119
There I, humble as I am, can give you the aid you want.

608
00:44:30,860 --> 00:44:33,779
I can set you your task from hour to hour.

609
00:44:34,320 --> 00:44:35,440
Stand by you always.

610
00:44:36,139 --> 00:44:38,039
Help you from moment to moment.

611
00:44:38,699 --> 00:44:40,500
This I could do in the beginning.

612
00:44:41,500 --> 00:44:45,244
Soon, for I know your powers, you would be as strong

613
00:44:45,244 --> 00:44:48,820
and apt as myself and would not require my help.

614
00:44:49,940 --> 00:44:53,740
But my powers, where are they for this undertaking?

615
00:44:54,339 --> 00:44:55,380
I do not feel them.

616
00:44:56,039 --> 00:44:58,960
Nothing speaks or stirs in me while you talk.

617
00:44:59,899 --> 00:45:03,346
I am sensible of no light kindling, no life

618
00:45:03,346 --> 00:45:06,921
quickening, no voice counselling or cheering.

619
00:45:07,899 --> 00:45:13,240
Oh, I wish I could make you see how much my mind is at this moment, like a rayless

620
00:45:13,240 --> 00:45:16,839
dungeon, with one shrinking fear fettered in its depths.

621
00:45:17,380 --> 00:45:21,199
The fear of being persuaded by you to attempt what I cannot accomplish.

622
00:45:22,539 --> 00:45:24,119
I have an answer for you.

623
00:45:24,460 --> 00:45:25,460
Hear it.

624
00:45:25,580 --> 00:45:28,419
I have watched you ever since we first met.

625
00:45:29,479 --> 00:45:32,119
I have made you my study for ten months.

626
00:45:33,139 --> 00:45:36,059
I have proved you in that time by sundry tests.

627
00:45:36,839 --> 00:45:38,860
And what have I seen and elicit it?

628
00:45:39,460 --> 00:45:45,119
In the village school, I found you could perform well, punctually, uprightly,

629
00:45:45,699 --> 00:45:49,039
labour, uncongenial to your habits and inclinations.

630
00:45:49,779 --> 00:45:53,160
I saw you could perform it with capacity and tact.

631
00:45:54,199 --> 00:45:56,179
You could win while you controlled.

632
00:45:57,139 --> 00:46:00,517
In the calm with which you learnt you had become

633
00:46:00,519 --> 00:46:04,240
suddenly rich, I read a mind clear of the vice of demass.

634
00:46:05,259 --> 00:46:10,500
Lucre had no undue power over you, in the resolute readiness with which you

635
00:46:10,501 --> 00:46:15,740
cut your wealth into four shares, keeping but one to yourself, and

636
00:46:15,740 --> 00:46:21,639
relinquishing the three others to the claim of abstract justice, I recognised a

637
00:46:21,641 --> 00:46:26,259
soul that reveled in the flame and excitement of sacrifice.

638
00:46:27,100 --> 00:46:32,800
In the tractability with which, at my wish, you forsook a study in which

639
00:46:32,801 --> 00:46:37,199
you were interested, and adopted another because it interested me.

640
00:46:38,300 --> 00:46:43,580
In the untiring aciduity with which you have since persevered in it, in the

641
00:46:43,581 --> 00:46:47,759
unflagging energy and unshaken temper with which you have met its difficulties,

642
00:46:48,259 --> 00:46:51,300
I acknowledge the complement of the qualities I seek.

643
00:46:52,059 --> 00:46:58,160
Jane, you are docile, diligent, disinterested, faithful, constant,

644
00:46:58,600 --> 00:47:04,100
and courageous, very gentle, and very heroic, cease to mistrust yourself,

645
00:47:04,740 --> 00:47:06,600
I can trust you unreservedly.

646
00:47:07,179 --> 00:47:10,308
As a conductress of Indian schools and a helper amongst

647
00:47:10,308 --> 00:47:13,619
Indian women, your assistance will be to me invaluable.

648
00:47:15,279 --> 00:47:21,119
My eye and shroud contracted around me, persuasion advanced with slow, sure step.

649
00:47:21,399 --> 00:47:23,380
Shut my eyes as I would.

650
00:47:23,940 --> 00:47:27,171
These last words of his succeeded in making the way,

651
00:47:27,172 --> 00:47:30,899
which had seemed blocked up, comparatively clear.

652
00:47:32,119 --> 00:47:38,220
My work, which had appeared so vague, so hopelessly diffuse, condensed itself as

653
00:47:38,221 --> 00:47:42,559
he proceeded, and assumed a definite form under his shaping hand.

654
00:47:43,220 --> 00:47:44,419
He waited for an answer.

655
00:47:45,419 --> 00:47:50,380
I demanded a quarter of an hour to think, before I again hazarded a reply.

656
00:47:50,940 --> 00:47:53,699
Very willingly, he rejoined.

657
00:47:54,399 --> 00:47:58,952
And rising, he strode a little distance up the pass, threw

658
00:47:58,953 --> 00:48:03,380
himself down on a swell of heath, and their lay still.

659
00:48:04,880 --> 00:48:07,259
I can do what he wants me to do.

660
00:48:08,179 --> 00:48:11,474
I am forced to see and acknowledge that, I

661
00:48:11,475 --> 00:48:16,221
am meditated, that is, if life be spared me.

662
00:48:16,339 --> 00:48:21,300
But I feel mine is not the existence to be long protracted under an Indian sun.

663
00:48:22,139 --> 00:48:23,139
What then?

664
00:48:23,639 --> 00:48:24,839
He does not care for that.

665
00:48:25,679 --> 00:48:30,179
When my time came to die, he would resign me, in all serenity and sanctity,

666
00:48:30,720 --> 00:48:31,899
to the God who gave me.

667
00:48:32,820 --> 00:48:34,660
The case is very plain before me.

668
00:48:35,539 --> 00:48:38,899
In leaving England, I should leave a loved but empty land.

669
00:48:39,500 --> 00:48:40,839
Mr. Rochester is not there.

670
00:48:41,369 --> 00:48:43,500
And if you were, what is?

671
00:48:44,139 --> 00:48:45,660
What can that ever be to me?

672
00:48:47,139 --> 00:48:49,259
My business is to live without him now.

673
00:48:49,919 --> 00:48:55,360
Nothing so absurd, so weak as to drag on from day to day, as if I were waiting some

674
00:48:55,361 --> 00:48:59,580
impossible change in circumstances which might reunite me to him.

675
00:49:00,559 --> 00:49:03,838
Of course, as Sinjin once said, I must seek

676
00:49:03,839 --> 00:49:07,080
another interest in life to replace the one lost.

677
00:49:08,160 --> 00:49:10,853
Is not the occupation he now offers me truly

678
00:49:10,854 --> 00:49:14,120
the most glorious man can adopt or God assign?

679
00:49:14,899 --> 00:49:20,940
Is it not, by its noble cares and sublime results, the one best calculated to fill

680
00:49:20,941 --> 00:49:24,100
the void left by up-torn affections and demolished hopes?

681
00:49:24,860 --> 00:49:29,059
I believe I must say, yes, and yet I shudder.

682
00:49:30,100 --> 00:49:34,240
Alas, if I join Sinjin, I abandon half myself.

683
00:49:35,080 --> 00:49:37,960
If I go to India, I go to premature death.

684
00:49:38,779 --> 00:49:41,717
And how will the interval between leaving England

685
00:49:41,718 --> 00:49:45,100
for India and India for the grave be filled?

686
00:49:45,979 --> 00:49:46,979
Oh, I know well.

687
00:49:47,899 --> 00:49:50,080
That too is very clear to my vision.

688
00:49:51,039 --> 00:49:56,520
By straining to satisfy Sinjin till my sin use ache, I shall satisfy him.

689
00:49:57,259 --> 00:50:01,720
To the finest central point and farthest outward circle of his expectations,

690
00:50:01,721 --> 00:50:09,120
if I do go with him, if I do make the sacrifice he urges, I will make it absolutely.

691
00:50:09,779 --> 00:50:14,759
I will throw all on the altar, heart, vitals, the entire victim.

692
00:50:15,960 --> 00:50:18,839
He will never love me, but he shall approve me.

693
00:50:19,440 --> 00:50:24,520
I will show him energies he has not yet seen, resources he has never suspected.

694
00:50:25,259 --> 00:50:28,919
Yes, I can work as hard as he can and with his little grudging.

695
00:50:30,160 --> 00:50:36,740
Consent then, to his demand is possible, but for one item, one dreadful item,

696
00:50:37,580 --> 00:50:43,179
it is, that he asks me to be his wife, and has no more of a husband's heart for

697
00:50:43,180 --> 00:50:45,816
me than that frowning giant of a rock down

698
00:50:45,817 --> 00:50:49,581
which the stream is foaming in Yonder gorge.

699
00:50:49,779 --> 00:50:54,380
He prizes me as a soldier would a good weapon, and that is all.

700
00:50:55,419 --> 00:50:58,479
Unmarried to him, this would never grieve me.

701
00:50:59,419 --> 00:51:04,039
But can I let him complete his calculations, call he put into practice

702
00:51:04,040 --> 00:51:06,679
his plans, go through the wedding ceremony?

703
00:51:07,860 --> 00:51:13,440
Can I receive from him the bridal ring, endure all the forms of love, which I

704
00:51:13,441 --> 00:51:19,419
doubt not, he would scrupulously observe, and know that the spirit was quite absent.

705
00:51:20,300 --> 00:51:24,243
Can I bear the consciousness that every endearment

706
00:51:24,244 --> 00:51:27,600
he bestows is a sacrifice made on principle?

707
00:51:27,960 --> 00:51:31,279
No, such a martyrdom would be monstrous.

708
00:51:31,839 --> 00:51:33,139
I will never undergo it.

709
00:51:33,679 --> 00:51:38,580
As his sister, I might accompany him, not as his wife, I will tell him so.

710
00:51:39,779 --> 00:51:44,699
I look towards the knoll, there he lay, still as a prostrate column.

711
00:51:45,320 --> 00:51:48,919
His face turned to me, his eye beaming watchful and keen.

712
00:51:49,679 --> 00:51:51,639
He started to his feet and approached me.

713
00:51:52,460 --> 00:51:55,179
I am ready to go to India, if I may go free.

714
00:51:56,360 --> 00:51:59,399
Your answer requires a commentary, he said.

715
00:52:00,179 --> 00:52:01,179
It is not clear.

716
00:52:03,000 --> 00:52:05,520
You have hitherto been my adopted brother.

717
00:52:06,080 --> 00:52:09,919
I, your adopted sister, let us continue as such.

718
00:52:10,399 --> 00:52:13,460
You and I had better not marry, he shook his head.

719
00:52:14,419 --> 00:52:16,779
Adopted fraternity will not do in this case.

720
00:52:17,720 --> 00:52:20,000
If you were my real sister, it would be different.

721
00:52:20,820 --> 00:52:23,240
I should take you and seek no wife.

722
00:52:24,240 --> 00:52:29,960
But as it is, either our union must be consecrated and sealed by marriage,

723
00:52:30,619 --> 00:52:31,979
or it cannot exist.

724
00:52:32,699 --> 00:52:35,779
Practical obstacles oppose themselves to any other plan.

725
00:52:36,679 --> 00:52:37,839
Do you not see it, Jane?

726
00:52:37,841 --> 00:52:39,220
Consider a moment.

727
00:52:39,660 --> 00:52:41,300
Your strong sense will guide you.

728
00:52:42,740 --> 00:52:43,740
I did consider.

729
00:52:44,580 --> 00:52:50,779
And still my sense, such as it was, directed me only to the fact that we did

730
00:52:50,781 --> 00:52:52,880
not love each other as man and wife should.

731
00:52:54,000 --> 00:52:56,960
And therefore, it inferred we ought not to marry.

732
00:52:57,559 --> 00:52:58,559
I said so.

733
00:52:59,520 --> 00:53:00,839
Sinjin, I returned.

734
00:53:01,699 --> 00:53:02,860
I regard you as a brother.

735
00:53:03,339 --> 00:53:05,880
You me as a sister, so let us continue.

736
00:53:07,020 --> 00:53:11,820
We cannot, we cannot, he answered, with short sharp determination.

737
00:53:12,899 --> 00:53:13,899
It would not do.

738
00:53:14,580 --> 00:53:16,339
You have said you will go with me to India.

739
00:53:17,080 --> 00:53:18,960
Remember, you have said that.

740
00:53:20,539 --> 00:53:21,539
Conditionally.

741
00:53:22,479 --> 00:53:28,380
Well, well, to the main point, the departure with me from England,

742
00:53:28,580 --> 00:53:31,160
the cooperation with me in my future labours.

743
00:53:31,580 --> 00:53:32,720
You do not object.

744
00:53:33,419 --> 00:53:36,399
You have already as good as put your hand to the plow.

745
00:53:37,039 --> 00:53:39,160
You are too consistent to withdraw it.

746
00:53:40,699 --> 00:53:42,839
You have but one end to keep in view.

747
00:53:43,860 --> 00:53:46,740
How the work you have undertaken can best be done.

748
00:53:48,160 --> 00:53:52,699
Simplify your complicated interests, feelings, thoughts, wishes, aims.

749
00:53:53,919 --> 00:53:58,119
Merge all considerations in one purpose that are fulfilling with effect,

750
00:53:58,699 --> 00:54:01,539
with power, the mission of your great master.

751
00:54:02,460 --> 00:54:06,899
To do so, you must have a coagitor, not a brother, that is a loose tie,

752
00:54:07,800 --> 00:54:08,800
but a husband.

753
00:54:09,539 --> 00:54:11,279
I too do not want a sister.

754
00:54:11,940 --> 00:54:13,800
A sister might any day be taken from me.

755
00:54:14,440 --> 00:54:15,440
I want a wife.

756
00:54:16,020 --> 00:54:18,472
The soul help me, I can influence efficiently

757
00:54:18,474 --> 00:54:21,380
in life and retain absolutely till death.

758
00:54:22,500 --> 00:54:23,899
I shuddered as he spoke.

759
00:54:24,940 --> 00:54:28,559
I felt his influence in my marrow, his hold on my limbs.

760
00:54:29,839 --> 00:54:32,600
Seek one elsewhere than in me, Sinjin.

761
00:54:33,479 --> 00:54:34,839
Seek one fitted to you.

762
00:54:36,100 --> 00:54:38,059
One fitted to my purpose, you mean?

763
00:54:38,679 --> 00:54:39,979
Fitted to my vocation.

764
00:54:40,979 --> 00:54:44,940
Again, I tell you, it is not the insignificant private individual,

765
00:54:44,941 --> 00:54:50,179
the mere man, with the man's selfish senses I wish to mate.

766
00:54:50,940 --> 00:54:52,240
It is the missionary.

767
00:54:53,660 --> 00:54:55,520
And I will give the missionary my energies.

768
00:54:56,139 --> 00:54:58,119
It is all he wants, but not myself.

769
00:54:59,160 --> 00:55:02,179
That would be only adding the husk and shell to the colonel.

770
00:55:02,899 --> 00:55:04,460
For them he has no use.

771
00:55:04,880 --> 00:55:05,880
I retain them.

772
00:55:07,220 --> 00:55:08,220
You cannot.

773
00:55:08,300 --> 00:55:09,300
You ought not.

774
00:55:10,160 --> 00:55:13,059
Do you think God will be satisfied with half an ablation?

775
00:55:13,660 --> 00:55:15,979
Will he accept a mutilated sacrifice?

776
00:55:17,000 --> 00:55:18,899
It is the cause of God I advocate.

777
00:55:19,679 --> 00:55:22,179
It is under his standard, I enlist you.

778
00:55:23,179 --> 00:55:25,820
I cannot accept on his behalf a divided allegiance.

779
00:55:26,580 --> 00:55:27,860
It must be entire.

780
00:55:29,339 --> 00:55:33,679
Oh, I will give my heart to God, I said, you do not want it.

781
00:55:35,360 --> 00:55:41,020
I will not swear, reader, that there was not something of repressed sarcasm,

782
00:55:41,419 --> 00:55:43,877
both in the tone in which I uttered this

783
00:55:43,879 --> 00:55:46,880
sentence and in the feeling that accompanied it.

784
00:55:47,360 --> 00:55:52,720
I had silently feared Syngin till now, because I had not understood him.

785
00:55:53,559 --> 00:55:56,940
He had held me in awe because he had held me in doubt.

786
00:55:58,139 --> 00:55:59,759
How much of him was saint?

787
00:56:00,539 --> 00:56:03,139
How much mortal I could not hear to foretell.

788
00:56:04,020 --> 00:56:06,860
But revelations were being made in this conference.

789
00:56:07,880 --> 00:56:11,500
The analysis of his nature was proceeding before my eyes.

790
00:56:11,501 --> 00:56:15,139
I saw his fallibilities, I comprehended them.

791
00:56:15,720 --> 00:56:21,699
I understood that, sitting there where I did, on the bank of Heath, and with that

792
00:56:21,701 --> 00:56:27,279
handsome form before me, I sat at the feet of a man, earing as I.

793
00:56:28,460 --> 00:56:31,139
The veil fell from his hardness and despotism.

794
00:56:31,979 --> 00:56:35,235
Having felt in him the presence of these qualities,

795
00:56:35,236 --> 00:56:38,040
I felt his imperfection and took courage.

796
00:56:38,300 --> 00:56:44,380
I was with an equal, one with whom I might argue, one whom, if I saw good,

797
00:56:44,899 --> 00:56:45,899
I might resist.

798
00:56:46,600 --> 00:56:49,948
He was silent after I had uttered the last sentence, and

799
00:56:49,948 --> 00:56:53,039
I presently risked an upward glance at his countenance.

800
00:56:54,059 --> 00:57:00,020
His eye, bent on me, expressed at once stern surprise and keen inquiry.

801
00:57:01,039 --> 00:57:04,960
Is she sarcastic and sarcastic to me, it seemed to say.

802
00:57:05,740 --> 00:57:07,399
What does this signify?

803
00:57:08,600 --> 00:57:11,300
Do not let us forget that this is a solemn matter.

804
00:57:11,919 --> 00:57:18,301
He said air long, one of which we may neither think nor talk lightly without sin.

805
00:57:18,899 --> 00:57:24,119
I trust, Jane, you are in earnest when you say you will serve your heart to God.

806
00:57:25,220 --> 00:57:26,360
It is all I want.

807
00:57:27,899 --> 00:57:33,740
Once rent your heart from man and fix it on your maker, the advancement of that

808
00:57:33,740 --> 00:57:39,199
maker's spiritual kingdom on earth will be your chief delight and endeavour.

809
00:57:40,339 --> 00:57:44,500
You will be ready to do at once whatever furthers that end.

810
00:57:45,399 --> 00:57:48,618
You will see what impetus would be given to your efforts

811
00:57:48,619 --> 00:57:52,039
and mine by our physical and mental union in marriage.

812
00:57:53,000 --> 00:57:56,830
The only union that gives a character of permanent

813
00:57:56,831 --> 00:58:01,000
conformity to the destinies and designs of human beings.

814
00:58:01,720 --> 00:58:08,300
And passing over all minor caprices or trivial difficulties and delicacies of

815
00:58:08,301 --> 00:58:12,770
feeling or scruple about the degree, kind, strength

816
00:58:12,771 --> 00:58:15,759
or tenderness of mere personal inclination.

817
00:58:16,360 --> 00:58:19,720
You will hasten to enter into that union at once.

818
00:58:21,039 --> 00:58:22,039
Shall I?

819
00:58:22,500 --> 00:58:23,500
I said briefly.

820
00:58:24,119 --> 00:58:27,517
And I looked at his features, beautiful in their harmony,

821
00:58:27,519 --> 00:58:30,300
but strangely formidable in their still severity.

822
00:58:31,059 --> 00:58:34,059
At his brow, commanding but not open.

823
00:58:34,720 --> 00:58:41,059
At his eyes, bright and deep and searching but never soft, at his tall imposing

824
00:58:41,061 --> 00:58:44,199
figure, and fancied myself in idea his wife.

825
00:58:45,160 --> 00:58:46,740
Oh, it would never do.

826
00:58:47,440 --> 00:58:50,080
As his curate, his comrade all would be right.

827
00:58:50,899 --> 00:58:53,220
I would cross oceans with him in that capacity.

828
00:58:54,399 --> 00:58:59,320
Toil under eastern suns, in Asian deserts with him in that office.

829
00:59:00,460 --> 00:59:03,699
Admire and emulate his courage and devotion and vigor.

830
00:59:04,720 --> 00:59:07,279
Accommodate quietly to his masterhood.

831
00:59:08,240 --> 00:59:11,600
Smile undisturbed at his ineradicable ambition.

832
00:59:12,600 --> 00:59:16,308
Discriminate the Christian from the man, profoundly

833
00:59:16,309 --> 00:59:19,100
esteem the one, and freely forgive the other.

834
00:59:20,059 --> 00:59:24,960
I should suffer often, no doubt, attached to him only in this capacity.

835
00:59:25,759 --> 00:59:31,559
My body would be under rather a stringent yoke, but my heart and mind would be free.

836
00:59:32,559 --> 00:59:35,979
I should still have my unblighted self to turn to.

837
00:59:36,779 --> 00:59:43,361
My natural, uninslaived feelings, with which to communicate in moments of loneliness.

838
00:59:44,100 --> 00:59:49,801
There would be recesses in my mind, which would be only mine, to which he never came.

839
00:59:50,339 --> 00:59:54,619
And sentiments growing there fresh and sheltered which his austerity could never

840
00:59:54,620 --> 00:59:58,800
blight, nor his measured warrior march trampled down.

841
00:59:59,619 --> 01:00:06,679
But as his wife, at his side always, and always restrained, and always checked,

842
01:00:07,259 --> 01:00:11,479
forced to keep the fire of my nature continually low, to compel it to burn

843
01:00:11,480 --> 01:00:14,641
inwardly and never utter a cry, though the

844
01:00:14,642 --> 01:00:18,080
imprisoned flame consumed vital after vital.

845
01:00:18,779 --> 01:00:21,479
This would be un-indurable.

846
01:00:23,179 --> 01:00:27,720
Singen, I exclaimed, when I had got so far in my meditation.

847
01:00:28,940 --> 01:00:31,259
Well, he answered Icily.

848
01:00:32,000 --> 01:00:34,721
I repeat, I freely consent to go with you as

849
01:00:34,721 --> 01:00:38,641
your fellow missionary, but not as your wife.

850
01:00:38,860 --> 01:00:41,119
I cannot marry you and become part of you.

851
01:00:42,139 --> 01:00:44,763
A part of me you must become, he answered

852
01:00:44,764 --> 01:00:48,861
steadily, otherwise the whole bargain is void.

853
01:00:49,520 --> 01:00:54,040
How can I, a man not yet 30, take out with me to

854
01:00:54,042 --> 01:00:58,061
India, a girl of 19, unless you be married to me?

855
01:00:58,660 --> 01:01:02,069
How can we be forever together, sometimes in

856
01:01:02,070 --> 01:01:06,539
solitudes, sometimes amidst savage tribes and unwed?

857
01:01:08,240 --> 01:01:11,240
Very well, I said shortly.

858
01:01:12,699 --> 01:01:17,423
Under the circumstances, quite as well as if I were either

859
01:01:17,425 --> 01:01:20,979
your real sister or a man and a clergyman like yourself.

860
01:01:22,139 --> 01:01:25,779
It is known that you are not my sister.

861
01:01:26,699 --> 01:01:31,220
I cannot introduce you as such, to attempt it would be too fast and

862
01:01:31,221 --> 01:01:36,520
injurious suspicions on us both, and for the rest, though you have a man's

863
01:01:36,520 --> 01:01:41,160
vigorous brain, you have a woman's heart, and it would not do.

864
01:01:42,179 --> 01:01:46,259
It would do, I affirmed with some disdain perfectly well.

865
01:01:46,820 --> 01:01:50,059
I have a woman's heart, but not where you are concerned.

866
01:01:50,759 --> 01:01:56,380
For you I have only a comrade's constancy, a fellow soldier's frankness, fidelity,

867
01:01:57,000 --> 01:02:02,540
fraternity if you like, a neophyte's respect and submission to his higher fount.

868
01:02:02,660 --> 01:02:04,539
Nothing more, don't fear.

869
01:02:05,380 --> 01:02:09,160
It is what I want, he said, speaking to himself.

870
01:02:09,800 --> 01:02:14,259
It is just what I want, and there are obstacles in the way.

871
01:02:14,399 --> 01:02:15,539
They must be tuned down.

872
01:02:16,559 --> 01:02:19,059
Jane, you would not repent marrying me.

873
01:02:19,139 --> 01:02:20,139
Be certain of that.

874
01:02:20,339 --> 01:02:21,339
We must be married.

875
01:02:21,740 --> 01:02:22,740
I repeat it.

876
01:02:23,160 --> 01:02:24,440
There is no other way.

877
01:02:25,259 --> 01:02:28,407
And undoubtedly, enough of love would follow upon

878
01:02:28,407 --> 01:02:32,479
marriage to render the union right even in your eyes.

879
01:02:33,679 --> 01:02:35,539
I scorn your idea of love.

880
01:02:36,320 --> 01:02:39,368
I could not help saying, as I rose up and stood

881
01:02:39,369 --> 01:02:42,880
before him, leaning my back against the rock.

882
01:02:43,139 --> 01:02:46,313
I scorned the counterfeit sentiment you offer,

883
01:02:46,315 --> 01:02:49,641
yes, engine, and I scorn you when you offer it.

884
01:02:49,940 --> 01:02:54,800
He looked at me fixately, compressing his well-cut lips while he did so.

885
01:02:56,080 --> 01:03:01,960
Whether he was incensed or surprised, or what, it was not easy to tell.

886
01:03:02,899 --> 01:03:05,020
He could command his countenance thoroughly.

887
01:03:06,839 --> 01:03:10,779
I scarcely expected to hear that expression from you, he said.

888
01:03:11,660 --> 01:03:15,160
I think I have done and uttered nothing to deserve scorn.

889
01:03:16,119 --> 01:03:21,440
I was touched by his gentle tone, and overroared by his high calm meon.

890
01:03:22,660 --> 01:03:23,899
Forgive me the words, engine.

891
01:03:24,839 --> 01:03:29,520
But it is your own fault that I have been roused to speak so unguardedly.

892
01:03:30,660 --> 01:03:34,139
You have introduced a topic on which our natures are at variance.

893
01:03:34,740 --> 01:03:38,157
A topic we should never discuss the very name

894
01:03:38,158 --> 01:03:41,520
of love is an apple of discord between us.

895
01:03:42,500 --> 01:03:45,520
If the reality were required, what should we do?

896
01:03:46,300 --> 01:03:47,300
How should we feel?

897
01:03:48,000 --> 01:03:51,860
My dear cousin abandoned your scheme of marriage, forget it.

898
01:03:52,520 --> 01:03:54,080
No, said he.

899
01:03:54,919 --> 01:04:00,460
It is a long cherished scheme, and the only one which can secure my great end.

900
01:04:00,600 --> 01:04:03,100
But I shall urge you no further at present.

901
01:04:04,759 --> 01:04:06,779
Tomorrow I leave home for Cambridge.

902
01:04:07,500 --> 01:04:10,740
I have many friends there to whom I should wish to say farewell.

903
01:04:11,419 --> 01:04:13,479
I shall be absent a fortnight.

904
01:04:14,419 --> 01:04:19,300
Take that space of time to consider my offer, and do not forget that if you

905
01:04:19,301 --> 01:04:22,779
reject it, it is not me you deny, but God.

906
01:04:23,880 --> 01:04:26,673
Through my means he opens to you a noble

907
01:04:26,675 --> 01:04:31,301
career, as my wife only can you enter upon it.

908
01:04:31,759 --> 01:04:35,422
Refuse to be my wife, and you limit yourself forever

909
01:04:35,423 --> 01:04:38,979
to a track of selfish ease and barren obscurity.

910
01:04:40,020 --> 01:04:42,703
Tremble less in that case you should be numbered with those

911
01:04:42,705 --> 01:04:46,380
who have denied the faith and are worse than infidel's.

912
01:04:47,639 --> 01:04:48,639
He had done.

913
01:04:49,660 --> 01:04:54,320
Turning from me, he once more looked to river, looked to hill.

914
01:04:55,500 --> 01:04:59,460
But this time, his feelings were all pent in his heart.

915
01:05:00,160 --> 01:05:02,600
I was not worthy to hear them uttered.

916
01:05:03,580 --> 01:05:09,080
As I walked by his side homeward, I read well in his iron silence all he

917
01:05:09,081 --> 01:05:13,872
felt towards me, the disappointment of an austere and despotic

918
01:05:13,873 --> 01:05:18,059
nature, which has met resistance where it expected submission.

919
01:05:18,759 --> 01:05:24,419
The disapprobation of a inflexible judgment which has detected in another

920
01:05:24,421 --> 01:05:28,759
feelings and views in which it has no power to sympathize.

921
01:05:29,100 --> 01:05:34,899
In short, as a man, he would have wished to coerce me into obedience.

922
01:05:35,779 --> 01:05:41,820
It was only as a sincere Christian he bore so patiently with my perversity and

923
01:05:41,820 --> 01:05:45,240
allowed so long a space for reflection and repentance.

924
01:05:46,119 --> 01:05:50,061
That night, after he had kissed his sisters, he

925
01:05:50,062 --> 01:05:53,460
thought proper to forget even to shake hands with me.

926
01:05:54,399 --> 01:05:55,880
But left the room in silence.

927
01:05:57,220 --> 01:06:03,300
I, who though I had no love, had much friendship for him, was hurt by the marked

928
01:06:03,301 --> 01:06:07,679
omission, so much hurt that tears started to my eyes.

929
01:06:09,119 --> 01:06:11,873
I see you and Syngin have been quarreling

930
01:06:11,875 --> 01:06:16,081
Jane, said Iana, during your walk on the more.

931
01:06:16,139 --> 01:06:17,139
But go after him.

932
01:06:17,820 --> 01:06:21,460
He is now lingering in the passage expecting you, he will make it up.

933
01:06:22,539 --> 01:06:25,399
I have not much pride under such circumstances.

934
01:06:26,259 --> 01:06:30,600
I would always rather be happy than dignified, and I ran after him.

935
01:06:31,500 --> 01:06:33,080
He stood at the foot of the stairs.

936
01:06:33,759 --> 01:06:36,160
Good night, Syngin, said I.

937
01:06:37,179 --> 01:06:38,179
Good night, Jane.

938
01:06:38,820 --> 01:06:39,820
He replied calmly.

939
01:06:40,979 --> 01:06:42,699
Then shake hands, I added.

940
01:06:43,580 --> 01:06:47,119
What a cold, loose touch he impressed on my fingers.

941
01:06:48,039 --> 01:06:50,880
He was deeply displeased by what had occurred that day.

942
01:06:51,520 --> 01:06:54,660
Cordiality would not warm, nor tears move him.

943
01:06:55,619 --> 01:06:58,399
No happy reconciliation was to be had with him.

944
01:06:59,220 --> 01:07:01,240
No cheering smile or generous word.

945
01:07:02,199 --> 01:07:06,020
But still, the Christian was patient and placid.

946
01:07:06,899 --> 01:07:11,960
And when I asked him if he forgave me, he answered that he was not in the habit

947
01:07:11,960 --> 01:07:17,000
of cherishing the remembrance of exation, that he had nothing to forgive,

948
01:07:17,639 --> 01:07:18,839
not having been offended.

949
01:07:19,839 --> 01:07:22,500
And with that answer, he left me.

950
01:07:23,639 --> 01:07:26,419
I would much rather he had knocked me down.
